meta {
  name: Update Referral Panel User
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-panels/{{referralPanelId}}/user
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "employeeName": "Panel One Updated",
    "email": "panel.one.updated@example.com",
    "mobileNumber": "9800000002",
    "address": "12 New Street"
  }
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `branch_admin:referrals__update_referral_panel`
  (`PERMISSION_KEYS.BR_REF_UPDATE_PANEL`) — the same permission `Update Referral
  Panel` requires.

  Update the referral panel's dedicated B2B ("B2B Referring Panel") login
  user's basic profile fields. All fields are optional (partial update).

  **Immutable / never accepted here** — branch, role, permissions/modules,
  status, and `username` (the login identifier) are all server-controlled and
  cannot be changed via this route. Unlike the regular staff `Update User`
  endpoint, `email` IS editable here, since a B2B login authenticates by
  `username`, not `email`.

  Sending `password` sets a new password immediately (bcrypt-hashed); omit it
  to leave the current password unchanged.

  Returns 404 `referral-panel` if the panel doesn't exist, or 404
  `referral-panel-user` if the panel has no login user yet (use *Create
  Referral Panel User* first). Uses `referralPanelId` captured by a *Create
  Referral Panel* request.
}
